## 10. Method notes and limitations

* Interpolation is inverse distance weighting; the power is selected by
  leave-one-out cross-validation and the selected surface is exact at sample points.
* Satellite land surface temperature is **surface**, not air, temperature. This is
  stated here for honesty; results describe the surface heat field.
* Residual spatial autocorrelation (Moran's I above) means the OLS p-values are
  optimistic; a spatial lag/error model is listed as future work.
* The cooling estimate is an indicative effect size from the regression, not a
  guaranteed outcome of planting.
* Out of scope: physical urban-climate simulation (WRF-UCM, ENVI-met), real-time
  sensor networks and 3D building models.

## 11. Future work

Kriging and regression-kriging, Random-Forest LST downscaling, multi-season and
time-of-day analysis, tree-planting scenario simulation, and integration with
population data.
